The main tail must remain intact: no favorable timing rerun or trimming was done. The complete per-callback arrays are in each `summary.json`.

## Exclusive sampled ancestry

The phase roots are direct, disjoint children of `updateBulk`; assignment is by descendant ancestry. HELD setter root is `set text` node 7 and publication root is Three.js `updateMatrixWorld` node 37. Main uses `set text` node 7 and `updateMatrixWorld` node 13. Root descendant sets do not overlap. Detached stacks are explicitly unresolved.

| Arm | Profile samples | Setter samples / self µs | Publication samples / self µs | Unresolved samples / self µs |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| HELD | 796 | 534 / 755,125 | 219 / 309,707 | 43 / 97,751 |
| Main | 3,750 | 407 / 690,582 | 3,211 / 5,703,124 | 132 / 285,836 |

The HELD setter exclusive stage buckets are JavaScript 146,081 µs, allocation 4,208 µs, host runtime 1,291 µs, shaping 226,211 µs, and other Wasm 377,334 µs. JavaScript plus allocation plus host runtime is a descriptive subset totaling 151,580 µs (1.895 ms per measured callback), not a compact-descriptor upper envelope: `other-wasm` also includes parsing, entry, and commit work. The category totals are profiler self-sample sums divided by 80 for description only, not savings. High's independent raw-frame sum identifies 39,668 µs in `frame-wire` JavaScript; 4,207 µs in `parse_update_request` plus `parse_text_mutations`; 16,127 µs in the named measure entry/wrapper (partly needed); 29,501 µs in `validate_planner_inputs` plus `validate_text_mutations`; and 13,833 µs in `commit_all` plus `commit_paragraphs` (needed). These are disjoint named self-sample totals, not removable-cost estimates; do not add them to broad stage totals or infer savings. JavaScript includes authoring work also needed on main, the allocation category is origin classification rather than bytes or exact allocation counts, and frozen source-map module labels do not provide dense semantic counters. High’s independent named-frame classification is preserved in `../current-cost-review.md` (SHA-256 `c525ea4748f76a321718047f47ee9d30c2a74a33517773c9ce57b4af182bdead`). It confirms the named sums are disjoint but not savings estimates. Raw frames and inputs are unchanged. No ABI or runtime candidate is selected.

The main setter phase is JavaScript-only (690,582 µs). Main publication is dominated by other Wasm (2,771,132 µs), shaping (1,052,074 µs), JavaScript (1,008,419 µs), gather (469,625 µs), and external JavaScript (194,875 µs). Exclusive sample buckets are not elapsed callback phases and should not be compared as marginal medians.

## Profile sample gaps and provenance

V8 `timeDeltas` are microseconds. Strictly greater than 5,000 µs: HELD 1 of 796 (37.125 ms); Main 77 of 3,750 (nearest-rank p50 7.042 ms, p90 16.000 ms, p95 28.125 ms, max 44.125 ms). Main gap bins are 46 at ≤8 ms, 11 in (8,12] ms, 16 in (12,20] ms, and 4 above 20 ms. All 77 over-threshold values are retained, converted to milliseconds, in `ancestry-preflight.json` and repeated in `callback-analysis.json`. These are profiler sample intervals, not callback-latency observations. Main also has 132 samples detached from either phase root (285,836 µs self sampled CPU), including 61 GC self samples (139,792 µs); HELD has 43 detached samples (97,751 µs), including inspector/GC/runtime activity. They remain unresolved, not reassigned to a phase.

Full node ancestry and raw URLs: `held-06fe/ancestry.json`, `main-4e25/ancestry.json`, and `ancestry-preflight.json`. Raw profiles are `held-06fe/cpu-profile.json` and `main-4e25/cpu-profile.json`; `summary/cpu-ancestry.md` preserves exclusive stage and named-frame tables. `manifest.json`, `postflight.json`, and per-arm preflight receipts retain exact identities and checks. No owned benchmark/build remains active; the existing unrelated Vite process was left untouched.

## Evidence correction and limits

`callback-analysis.json` was corrected after detecting that an initial calculation had labeled raw microseconds as milliseconds and used the wrong threshold. It now records units, strict `>5000µs` count, max, and the complete correctly converted value list from `ancestry-preflight.json`; SHA-256 `3af6f939d7f6b1a7931c04baf111923a02e43e3edb21484e5f2b2d9e993fc53d`. Raw profile files were not changed. This one pair is a current-artifact diagnostic only: the main tail makes pair-wide ranking unsuitable for causal budget or parity claims, and no counterfactual establishes savings.
